  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>This dog wash, run by the Speed Laverie brand (registered business, SIRET 901 474 130 00076), is located on avenue Jean d'Agrève, in the harbour area of Hyères. A self-service station designed to wash and dry your dog in a few minutes, without going through a traditional grooming salon.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The station runs self-service, 24 hours a day, 7 days a week, confirmed by the official Speed Laverie website and several independent directories (laverie24.fr, annuaire-entreprises.data.gouv.fr). The price is €10 for the first 10 minutes, then €2 per additional 2-minute block. The exact street number on avenue Jean d'Agrève varies slightly between the directories consulted — once in the area, look out for the machine dedicated to dogs, which is separate from the regular launderette.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the area combines a regular launderette with the dog wash — bring change or your card depending on the payment method accepted on the machine.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The Hyères harbour and its beaches are right nearby — so you can combine a swim and a rinse without much of a trip: the <a href="fiche-hyeres-merou">beach between L'Ayguade and Les Salins</a>, the <a href="fiche-balade-giens">Giens peninsula</a>, or the <a href="fiche-camping-mediterranee-hyeres">Camping Méditerranée</a> if you're staying overnight nearby (these three pages are only available in French for now).</p>
    </div>

